Round 1: The Qualifying Round (Frontend) — Online:

Date: 12th September 2026
Duration: 24 Hours
Submission Deadline: 13th September 2026
Mode: Online
Description:

Participants will receive a problem statement along with the required resources and guidelines.
The objective of Round 1 is to design and develop a complete, functional website within 24 hours.
Participants will be expected to work on both the frontend and backend, implementing the required features and functionality described in the problem statement.
The final submission should be a complete working website with the required features properly implemented.
The judging criteria, feature requirements, marks distribution, and submission guidelines will be provided along with the problem statement.
Only the top-performing participants/teams will qualify for Round 2.
Round 2: The Finale — Offline:

The qualifiers from Round 1 will advance to Round 2, which will be conducted offline.
The problem statement, schedule, duration, requirements, and detailed guidelines for Round 2 will be shared with the qualified participants after the completion of Round 1.
Participants should be prepared for a challenging and exciting finale that will push their creativity, technical skills, and ability to build under pressure.
